# What lands on disk is a property of the commit, not of the clone.
#
# Without this file core.autocrlf decides, and it decided differently in
# different places: the main checkout held LF while every .claude worktree
# checked out CRLF, so at one identical HEAD `tools/build_paper_b.py --check`
# passed in one and reported a stale build in the other. The paper gates now
# normalise before hashing, which is the repair that matters; this file removes
# the divergence they are normalising around, so a digest taken over raw bytes
# is not a trap waiting for the next person to set it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries. `binary` is the macro for `-text -diff`: git neither rewrites line
# endings nor tries to diff them. Listing them by extension matters because
# git's own text/binary heuristic samples only the first 8000 bytes for a NUL
# and two files here have none. docs/theory/rewrite_calculus_note.pdf was
# already being checked out 1843 bytes longer than its blob, with its xref
# offsets broken; data/research/juggler/excursion_transfer/excursions.bin
# survives today only because it happens to contain no lone LF, and would be
# corrupted the same way as soon as its contents change.
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.zip     binary
*.bin     binary
*.parquet binary

# cmd.exe is the one consumer that still wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
